        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "About The Old School House, Ballycumber South, Tinahely, Tinahely, Co. Wicklow\r\nDescription\r\n\r\nMcDonnell Properties are delighted to bring to the market Ballycumber School House, a property of immense character and charm, set in a beautiful rural location in the heart of County Wicklow in the middle of the Wicklow Way.\r\n\r\nOriginally serving as a local schoolhouse, this unique property offers a wonderful opportunity for those seeking a home with history, character and a strong connection to its surrounding countryside. The property enjoys a tranquil setting surrounded by the rolling Wicklow countryside, while remaining within easy reach of Tinahely and its excellent range of local amenities. The surrounding area is renowned for its scenic beauty, offering an idyllic lifestyle away from the hustle and bustle of city living. Approached via a charming stone avenue and gated entrance, the property immediately evokes a wonderful sense of privacy and arrival. Steps lead into the welcoming entrance foyer, with access to the basement located on either side. The property benefits from its own well water. It has its own septic tank and oil heating.\r\n\r\nThe Accommodation\r\nInternally, Ballycumber School House retains a wealth of original character and charm, with generous room proportions and features that reflect its former use and heritage. The property presents an exciting opportunity for a new owner to thoughtfully restore and transform the accommodation into a truly distinctive home.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor begins with a welcoming foyer measuring approximately 13.9 ft x 9.3 ft, featuring an original wood-burning stove which immediately sets the tone for the character found throughout the property.\r\n\r\nTo the left of the foyer, lead to a versatile study or lounge measuring approximately 9 ft x 13 ft. This room also benefits from its own original wood-burning stove, creating a cosy and inviting space.\r\n\r\nFrom here, you enter the impressive main living room, measuring approximately 24.9 ft x 14.4 ft. This substantial room enjoys excellent proportions, another stove and access to the rear of the property. Previously used as the principal living area, its generous footprint offers enormous versatility and could readily be reimagined to suit a variety of modern lifestyles.\r\n\r\nTo the opposite side of the foyer lies the spacious kitchen/dining room, measuring approximately 25.15 ft x 14.8 ft. A fantastic entertaining space, the room features an original stove set within a tiled fireplace, together with cabinetry incorporating tongue-and-groove detailing. With its impressive proportions and abundance of character, this room offers considerable scope for a new owner to create a superb contemporary country kitchen and dining area, subject to the necessary works and permissions.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the sleeping accommodation is approached via a charming landing measuring approximately 16.8 ft x 5.2 ft, with windows providing excellent natural light.\r\n\r\nBedroom One measures approximately 13 ft x 9.8 ft and features attractive grey oak flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom Two is a generous and versatile space, incorporating areas measuring approximately 14 ft x 10 ft and 10 ft x 7 ft. The room is fully carpeted and benefits from a skylight, allowing natural light to flood the space.\r\n\r\nThe attic is also accessed from the first floor, providing additional potential for storage or future use, subject to the necessary planning permissions and building requirements.\r\n\r\nThroughout the property, the accommodation benefits from double-glazed windows and traditional window shutters, complementing the property’s period character.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nThe surrounding grounds further enhance the appeal of this wonderful country property sitting on 1/3 of an acre. The generous setting provides excellent potential for creating beautiful gardens where there are currently apple trees growing, outdoor entertaining areas in the private patio private spaces from which to enjoy the surrounding Wicklow countryside.\r\n\r\nFor those with vision, the grounds and existing accommodation offer an exciting opportunity to further enhance and personalise the property, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nA Home Full of Potential\r\nBallycumber School House is a truly unique property where character, history and potential come together. Whether you are looking to create a distinctive family home, a peaceful countryside retreat, a weekend escape or a property to sensitively restore and put your own stamp on, this former schoolhouse provides an exceptional blank canvas.\r\n\r\nProperties of this nature and setting rarely come to the market. With its original features, generous accommodation, wonderful rural surroundings and position along the Wicklow Way, Ballycumber School House offers the discerning purchaser an opportunity to create something genuinely special.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the character, setting, proportions and enormous potential this wonderful property has to offer"
      },
